# Drop your corporate root CA PEM here (Zscaler, Palo Alto, Symantec, etc.)
# and restart the core service. OpenVox will trust it for outbound HTTPS.
#
# To find your corporate root on macOS:
#   security find-certificate -a -p /Library/Keychains/System.keychain > extra-ca.pem
# On Linux: /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. The file is read by openvox-core on startup
# (see OPENVOX_EXTRA_CA_FILE in .env.example).
